WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.309
<v Waiver Operations Lead>I raised a real problem with the new guidance, and

00:00:03.309 --> 00:00:06.617
<v Waiver Operations Lead>the response was that operations always wants exceptions. That was

00:00:06.617 --> 00:00:09.264
<v Waiver Operations Lead>not about the rule. That was about me.

00:00:09.614 --> 00:00:12.626
<v Human Services Supervisor>You are right that the comment was about motives. I

00:00:12.626 --> 00:00:15.637
<v Human Services Supervisor>should have redirected it in the meeting. Can I separate

00:00:15.637 --> 00:00:18.649
<v Human Services Supervisor>the strands with you? What is the work question underneath

00:00:18.649 --> 00:00:18.950
<v Human Services Supervisor>this?

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.027
<v Waiver Operations Lead>Whether the rule applies to plans that were already approved.

00:00:23.027 --> 00:00:25.636
<v Waiver Operations Lead>If it does, about 300 plans stall.

00:00:25.986 --> 00:00:30.131
<v Human Services Supervisor>That is a fair question, and it is answerable. Research

00:00:30.131 --> 00:00:34.276
<v Human Services Supervisor>on teams separates three kinds of conflict. Disagreement about the

00:00:34.276 --> 00:00:38.421
<v Human Services Supervisor>work, friction between people, and disputes about who does what.

00:00:38.421 --> 00:00:42.566
<v Human Services Supervisor>The personal and process kinds are reliably linked to worse

00:00:42.566 --> 00:00:45.882
<v Human Services Supervisor>performance. Disagreement about the work is more mixed.

00:00:46.232 --> 00:00:49.472
<v Waiver Operations Lead>Mixed how? I thought debate was supposed to be healthy.

00:00:49.822 --> 00:00:53.966
<v Human Services Supervisor>A meta-analysis of 116 studies found no overall link between

00:00:53.966 --> 00:00:58.111
<v Human Services Supervisor>task conflict and performance. In teams below top management, it

00:00:58.111 --> 00:01:02.255
<v Human Services Supervisor>was actually negative. It was most harmful when it came

00:01:02.255 --> 00:01:06.400
<v Human Services Supervisor>bundled with personal friction, which is what happened in that

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:06.814
<v Human Services Supervisor>meeting.

00:01:07.164 --> 00:01:10.204
<v Waiver Operations Lead>So the problem is not that I disagreed. It is

00:01:10.204 --> 00:01:13.244
<v Waiver Operations Lead>that the disagreement turned into a fight about who cares

00:01:13.244 --> 00:01:14.460
<v Waiver Operations Lead>more about the rules.

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:18.362
<v Human Services Supervisor>Yes. One study of 70 leadership teams found that when

00:01:18.362 --> 00:01:21.914
<v Human Services Supervisor>trust is low, people read a challenge to their idea

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:25.466
<v Human Services Supervisor>as a challenge to them. That probably happened on both

00:01:25.466 --> 00:01:29.018
<v Human Services Supervisor>sides. I suspect the policy specialist heard your concern as

00:01:29.018 --> 00:01:30.794
<v Human Services Supervisor>an attack on their work.

00:01:31.144 --> 00:01:33.496
<v Waiver Operations Lead>I can see that. What happens now?

00:01:33.846 --> 00:01:37.595
<v Human Services Supervisor>I will route the interpretation question to the person or

00:01:37.595 --> 00:01:41.345
<v Human Services Supervisor>area responsible for the rule. Then I will bring you

00:01:41.345 --> 00:01:45.094
<v Human Services Supervisor>and the policy specialist together with a narrow agenda: the

00:01:45.094 --> 00:01:48.843
<v Human Services Supervisor>question, the evidence, who decides, and by when. Comments about

00:01:48.843 --> 00:01:50.718
<v Human Services Supervisor>motives stay off the table.

00:01:51.068 --> 00:01:54.805
<v Waiver Operations Lead>And the call-line representative? They raised the same concern and

00:01:54.805 --> 00:01:56.300
<v Waiver Operations Lead>stopped coming to briefings.

00:01:56.650 --> 00:02:00.104
<v Human Services Supervisor>They come back. Their callers will live with the result.

00:02:00.104 --> 00:02:03.557
<v Human Services Supervisor>The evidence on people being pushed out after disagreeing is

00:02:03.557 --> 00:02:07.011
<v Human Services Supervisor>thinner, but it points the same way. Losing the person

00:02:07.011 --> 00:02:10.465
<v Human Services Supervisor>who disagrees usually means losing information the team will need

00:02:10.465 --> 00:02:10.810
<v Human Services Supervisor>later.
